notes

# Built site output. Netlify runs `npm run check && npm run build` on every
# deploy (netlify.toml), so the served site is always generated from the
# source that produced it — there's no reason to carry the generated HTML,
# markdown mirrors, component bundle, or copied examples in git.
#
# The `v<version>/` directories are the deliberate exception, and they are
# NOT build output: scripts/build-site.js preserves them across rebuilds and
# never regenerates an older one (see its own comment — "URLs are public
# contracts — we MUST NOT blow them away on rebuild"). They are the
# immutable published artifacts every released `$id` and `$schema` URL
# resolves against, and /stability promises each stays "frozen at the bytes
# it shipped with". Ignoring them would 404 every version before the current
# one. They stay tracked.
/site/dist/*
!/site/dist/v[0-9]*
